34868.sol:
Given differential equation is

$\frac{d y}{d x}+\frac{2}{x} \cdot$ y=x²

This is of the linear form.

$\begin{aligned}$& \therefore P=$\frac{2}{x},$ Q=x² \\
& $\text{ I.F }=$ e^{$\int \frac{2}{x}$ d x}=e^{$\log x$²}=x²
\end{aligned}

Solution is

$\begin{aligned}$& y $\cdot$ x^2=$\int$ x^2 $\cdot$ x^2 d x+c=$\frac{x^5}{5}+$ c \\
& y=$\frac{x^3}{5}+$ c x^{-2}
\end{aligned}

